&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qui sommes-nous ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Artefact est un cabinet de conseil international spécialisé en Data et Intelligence Artificielle, présent dans plus de 20 pays avec plus de 2 500 collaborateurs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous accompagnons nos clients dans leur transformation en combinant expertise technologique, conseil et connaissance métier, sur des enjeux allant de la stratégie Data &amp;amp; IA à la conception et au déploiement de solutions concrètes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nos équipes réunissent notamment des Business Consultants, Data Analysts, Data Scientists et Data Engineers, qui interviennent auprès de grands groupes internationaux dans des secteurs variés.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Notre ambition : mettre la Data et l’IA au service de problématiques business concrètes et créer un impact mesurable pour nos clients.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ton rôle&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Au sein de l’équipe Talent Acquisition France et sous la responsabilité de la Head of Talent Acquisition, tu pilotes en autonomie le recrutement des équipes Strat Data d’Artefact, sur des profils allant de Junior à Manager.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partenaire des équipes opérationnelles, tu les accompagnes tout au long du processus afin de garantir des recrutements de qualité et une expérience candidat exigeante :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Piloter les recrutements de bout en bout&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Recueillir et challenger les besoins auprès des managers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Définir et mettre en œuvre l’approche de recrutement adaptée à chaque besoin&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Piloter l’ensemble du processus : sourcing, qualification, entretiens RH, coordination des étapes d’évaluation et offre&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développer une approche proactive du sourcing et constituer des viviers de profils pertinents.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Accompagner les équipes opérationnelles&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conseiller et challenger les managers tout au long du processus afin de garantir des décisions de recrutement objectives et cohérentes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Garantir la bonne application du processus et des méthodes d’évaluation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Veiller à une expérience de recrutement de qualité pour les candidatures et les équipes internes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Contribuer à l’amélioration continue&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identifier les points de friction et contribuer à l’amélioration des processus et pratiques&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Veiller à la qualité et à la fiabilité des données dans notre ATS (Greenhouse)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribuer aux projets et initiatives de l’équipe Talent Acquisition.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Ton profil&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une expérience confirmée en recrutement, idéalement dans le conseil/ ESN&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une maîtrise du recrutement de bout en bout, avec une solide pratique du sourcing et de l’approche directe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une capacité à gérer et prioriser un périmètre de recrutement en autonomie&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une posture de business partner, avec la capacité de conseiller et challenger&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une bonne maîtrise des outils de recrutement et un bon niveau d’anglais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Rémunération : &lt;/strong&gt;jusqu’à 44K annuel selon profil.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Formations continues et participation à des projets stratégiques d&#39;acquisition et de fidélisation des talents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Équipe dynamique, flexibilité télétravail, séminaires d&#39;équipe&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Localisation Paris 9ème&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Étapes du recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ol&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entretien avec Mélody, Head of Talent Acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Entretien avec Laurie, DRH&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Chez Artefact, nous recrutons nos collaborateurs uniquement en fonction de nos besoins et des qualités propres de chaque candidat. Nous assurons le développement de leurs compétences professionnelles et de leurs responsabilités sans discrimination d’aucune sorte, notamment de croyances, de genre, d’âge, de situation d&#39;handicap, d’origine ethnique, d’orientation sexuelle, d’appartenance à une organisation politique, religieuse, syndicale ou à une minorité.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3 id=&quot;isPasted&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Company Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrea delivers effects-as-a-service to national security partners across five domains and more than a dozen mission areas. These include airborne ISR, electronic warfare, secure communications, aerial refueling, special air missions, aerial firefighting, and advanced simulation. We own the whole stack: designing, building, and operating turnkey capabilities that give our partners decisive, asymmetric advantage against rapidly evolving threats.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our operating model is built around three interlocking pillars. The Support Groups provide a global shared-service – spanning people, finance, platform, operations, legal, and engagement. This frees up our Core Groups, who develop and own mission capabilities end-to-end, to focus entirely on delivery. The Market Groups apply a regional lens, ensuring that our agile and adaptable capabilities remain aligned to the wicked problems that matter most to our partners across the Americas, EMEA, and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At the heart of our model is a simple but powerful idea: be a true partner with skin in the game. Our partners need effects, not just equipment. By owning the full stack – from the lab to the field – we are able to drive a continuous cycle of innovation that keeps our partners ahead. It&#39;s a fast-moving, intellectually demanding environment where talented people are given real responsibility, work on problems that matter, and contribute to an enterprise that is growing quickly and deliberately.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Headquartered in Washington, DC, with facilities across the United States, the United Kingdom, as well as Continental Europe and Asia-Pacific.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Group Overview&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Digital and Synthetic Capability Unit (D&amp;amp;S) is committed to providing mission-driven information solutions that seamlessly bridge the digital and physical realms. Leveraging cutting-edge technologies and advanced platforms, we empower operational readiness and elevate situational awareness across diverse domains—including air, maritime, and space.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position Summary&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrea is seeking a dynamic and highly motivated individual to join our software development team, building business software solutions and visualisations for the Enterprise.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design, implement, and maintain well-tested, scalable code in alignment with our engineering principles and standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead the delivery of features and enhancements to production, coordinating cross-functionally where needed&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Architect, design, and implement microservices or monolithic solutions to improve functionality and performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apply strong understanding of system architecture and design patterns to propose and implement effective technical solutions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Troubleshoot, debug and resolve production issues, including conducting root cause analysis and implementing preventative improvements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively contribute to code reviews, providing constructive feedback to uphold and elevate overall code quality across the team&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate effectively with teammates and stakeholders, contributing to technical discussions and leading design decisions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify technical debt, performance bottlenecks and architectural improvements, and drive initiatives to address them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Consistently adhere to and help reinforce our Ways of Working, contributing to process improvements where appropriate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communicate progress, risks and trade-offs clearly to the team and relevant stakeholders to ensure alignment with the product roadmap&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6 years of experience as a backend engineer with a strong focus on web development, REST APIs and software architecture ideally with Python frameworks&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;BSc level qualification in Software Engineering or equivalent Computer Science related discipline&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding and practical experience of web development using Python Frameworks e.g. Django/FastAPI&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with cloud technologies, preferably Azure, and tools like Kafka, Docker, Kubernetes, Elasticsearch&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Understanding and/or experience of team delivery in an Agile software development environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive to learn constantly and further your knowledge&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong leadership, organisational skills, proactive approach to task delivery and required documentation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Great interpersonal skills, able to confidently communicate and articulate technical issues to non-technical team members&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Private Medical Insurance  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Subsided gym membership / plans through Wellhub  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Electric Car scheme  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cycle to work scheme  &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Free lunch on office days &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced Parental Leave &lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;30 days annual PTO plus b/h&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bonus Scheme&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Personal development opportunities&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work&amp;nbsp;Authorization&amp;nbsp;/&amp;nbsp;Security&amp;nbsp;Clearance&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;TextRun SCXW169204765 BCX8&quot; lang=&quot;EN-US&quot; data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;&lt;span class=&quot;NormalTextRun SCXW169204765 BCX8&quot;&gt;The employee will have the legal right to work in the United Kingdom and will be able to produce right to work documentation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;Employee must undergo a minimum of BPSS check.&amp;nbsp;Employee must be willing to sign the Official Secrets Act.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;AAP/EEO Statement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Metrea is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Employment decisions are made without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, or other characteristics protected by law. &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Position&amp;nbsp;Type&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;Expected&amp;nbsp;Hours&amp;nbsp;of&amp;nbsp;Work&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a full-time non-exempt position with typical working hours of Monday through Friday, 9:00 a.m. to 6:00 p.m. Hours and work shifts may change in accordance with department and business needs. Exempt Employees must have the ability to be on-call and available, as business needs require. Non-Exempt employees may be required to work over 40 hours per week with approval from the department manager.  &lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Work&amp;nbsp;Environment&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This job operates on a hybrid working split, with a requirement of three days per week of office-based work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role may require occasional travel to other Metrea UK offices.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Our Firmware&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Metrea, our single core value is Rooted in Humility, and our four cornerstone attributes are Entrepreneurial, Systematic, Discerning, and Over-Deliver. These form what we call our Teammate Firmware. Just like technical firmware connects software and hardware, our Firmware is the constant interface between our mission and our people. It defines how we show up, how we work together, and how we solve complex problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our team Firmware creates a web-like, hyper-collaborative, dynamically hierarchical way of working that helps us adapt quickly, communicate openly, and distribute decision-making to where expertise actually lives. It enables groups to self-organize around hard problems, shift fluidly as priorities evolve, and operate with the trust, curiosity, and discipline required in a complex mission space. This foundation allows us to deliver elegant, effective solutions and uphold our purpose: protecting our precious inheritance.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Established in 2004, &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;OLIVER&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; is the world’s first and only specialist in designing, building, and running bespoke in-house agencies and marketing ecosystems for brands. We partner with over 300 clients in 40+ countries and counting. Our unique model drives creativity and efficiency, allowing us to deliver tailored solutions that resonate deeply with audiences.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;As a part of &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;The Brandtech Group&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;, we&#39;re at the forefront of leveraging cutting-edge AI technology to revolutionise how we create and deliver work. Our &lt;/span&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;none&quot;&gt;AI solutions&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt; enhance efficiency, spark creativity, and drive insightful decision-making, empowering our teams to produce innovative and impactful results.&lt;/span&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Role: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233279&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;Regional Operations Director (EMEA)&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;Location: &lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;London, United Kingdom&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt; &lt;strong&gt;(3 days a week from our London offices)&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;About the role:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;The Regional Operations Director is accountable for the operational effectiveness of the EMEA region. Reporting to the Global Chief Transformation and Operations Officer, you&#39;ll translate the global operating model into practical, market-specific execution — building the structure, governance and performance focus needed to strengthen operational control and support scalable growth.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;You&#39;ll lead a regional operations team, partner closely with regional and global leadership, and act as the key connector between regional execution and global capability. The role calls for a leader equally comfortable setting strategic direction and solving complex operational problems hands-on — someone who turns data into action, builds high-performing teams, and keeps commercial performance firmly in focus.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you will be doing:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;335559739&amp;quot;:240}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional operational leadership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Set clear priorities, accountabilities and ways of working for the EMEA Regional Operations function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build the structure, rhythm and capability needed to improve client delivery, business performance and regional growth.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the senior operational partner to Regional Leadership on risks, performance, capacity and improvement priorities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Client delivery operations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the operational run model for EMEA clients — including cadence, governance, issue resolution and escalation management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Leadership to ensure delivery risks are visible, blockers are resolved quickly and client teams are set up to deliver effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regional clients are mobilised and supported through consistent operating standards and reliable delivery controls.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Governance, cadence and decision management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the regional governance rhythm: forums, communications, decision-making and performance reviews.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure decisions are made at the right level, escalations are routed effectively and regional context is represented in relevant global and regional forums.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive clear actions, accountability and follow-through across the function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Operating model execution&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embed the global operating model across EMEA, ensuring standards, processes, tools and governance expectations are adopted consistently.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate enterprise-level standards into practical, market-specific ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Resource and capacity management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the regional view of demand, supply, utilisation, resource mix and capacity gaps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Global Capacity Management, Account Teams, Delivery Leads and Offshore Operations to optimise deployment, resolve constraints and improve utilisation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regional input into enterprise workforce planning and future capacity needs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Business and client enablement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure regional client teams have the operational foundations needed to mobilise and deliver work effectively.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate core business processes including client onboarding, timesheeting, billing readiness, interagency set-ups, compliance and headcount approvals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the regional operational point of coordination for enablement issues, working across Finance, HR, Technology and Implementation to unblock dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial performance and margin management&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage the operational levers that affect cost-to-serve across the region, including scope leakage, resource efficiency, rework and avoidable cost.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner with Account Leadership and Finance to improve margin visibility and ensure practical actions are in place to protect profitable delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee regional budget performance and present financial outcomes to regional and global stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Regional insight and continuous improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use performance data to identify risks, issues and improvement opportunities across the region.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Translate insight into action — ensuring key issues have clear owners, measurable outcomes and appropriate escalation routes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify recurring operational bottlenecks and lead remediation, including regional adoption of global improvement initiatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-functional partnership&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the key operational connector between EMEA and global operations capabilities.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner across Sales, Account, Implementation, Finance, HR, Technology and Offshore functions to drive client outcomes and operational consistency.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide regional operational input into sales pursuits, client mobilisation, scope expansions and solution design — ensuring proposed models are deliverable and scalable.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Interface with Global Programme Directors where regional and global client contexts intersect, aligning on dependencies, escalations and capacity impacts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team leadership and development&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead, coach and develop the Regional Operations team, building a high-performing function with clear roles, standards and ways of working.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Foster a culture of accountability, collaboration, operational discipline and continuous improvement.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure the team has the skills, confidence and behaviours needed to support a more mature, insight-led and scalable delivery model.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;What you need to be great in this role:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{&amp;quot;134233117&amp;quot;:true,&amp;quot;134233118&amp;quot;:true}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;Essential&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Senior operations leadership experience within, advertising, consulting, creative production, media agency or professional services.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep understanding of agency operating models — including client delivery, workflow, resource planning, utilisation, scopes of work, billing, compliance and margin management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven experience leading regional or multi-market operations teams in a people-led, fast-paced environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong commercial acumen, with confidence managing the operational levers that affect profitability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience owning or improving resource and capacity management, including demand and supply visibility, workforce mix and deployment planning.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to use operational data, KPIs and reporting to identify risks, drive action and improve performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record embedding governance, process discipline and ways of working across complex teams or markets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong cross-functional stakeholder skills — with experience partnering across regional and global functions including Finance, HR, Technology, Account and Delivery.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven people leadership: building capable teams, strengthening operational performance and creating a culture of accountability.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable moving between strategic direction and hands-on operational problem-solving.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Desirable&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in a global matrix organisation with regional, global and offshore delivery models.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in an in-house agency, embedded agency, creative production or complex marketing ecosystem.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to client mobilisation, implementation, transition or new operating model design.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience contributing to RFPs, commercial modelling, solution design or delivery model development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to automation, AI-enabled operations, workflow optimisation or digital transformation in a marketing or agency environment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p class=&quot;mb-2 whitespace-pre-wrap&quot;&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commercial and budget accountability&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing regional or annual operational budgets and presenting financial performance to senior stakeholders.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track record of driving margin discipline — reducing leakage, rework and avoidable cost across complex delivery environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to connect operational decisions to commercial outcomes and communicate financial performance clearly to leadership.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strategic integration of AI tools to improve operational efficiency, insight and reporting across a regional function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience setting AI governance standards and embedding AI-assisted workflows within a team or function.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Agentic leadership approach: systematic, outcome-oriented problem-solving across complex, multi-stakeholder environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Confidence driving AI adoption and sharing best practice across a broader operations network.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong judgment in evaluating AI outputs and maintaining rigorous human oversight.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
